<main class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md border border-[#C1C1C1] max-w-xl mx-auto">
    <form action="<%= formAction %>" method="POST" enctype="multipart/form-data" class="space-y-5">
        
        <!-- Label -->
        <label for="image" class="block hover:rotate-3 text-lg font-semibold text-[#1F1F1F]">
            📷 Upload Your Art or Profile Image
        </label>
    
        <!-- File Input -->
        <input type="file" name="image" accept="image/*"
                class="block w-full text-[#1F1F1F] file:mr-4 file:py-2 file:px-4
                        file:rounded-md file:border-0
                        file:text-sm file:font-semibold
                        file:bg-[#7E5DFA] file:text-white
                        hover:file:bg-[#6844e0] transition-all duration-200" />
    
        <!-- Submit Button -->
        <button type="submit"
                class="w-full bg-[#7E5DFA] text-white font-bold py-2 px-4 rounded-md
                        hover:bg-[#6844e0] hover:scale-105 transition-all duration-300">
            🚀 Upload Image
        </button>
    </form>
</main>
    



<!-- 
Apply this for whenyou add to ejs, not in actual partial. 

I wanted to make reusable pieces for ejs. So they can actually be utilized. when there is a form you have to use formAction with beestings <formAction%> , when you "include" it on an ejs sheet use <include(action="<formAction%>" when you add it to the ejs use BEESTING- include('../partials/uploadForm', {formAction:'routepath'})BEESTING)-->